WEBVTT

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:08.100
What the? What is this?!

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.260
How come I'm in pieces?

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.220
Am I dead?

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.140
Or am I alive?

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.180
What happened to me?

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.760
I can't remember anything!

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:20.300
Who am I?

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:26.260
I don't know. What is my name?

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.640
Dammit!

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:58.180
I'm in pieces, but they're connected.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:01.850
Was I fragmented in order for
me to put the pieces together?

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:04.260
Who would do that to me?

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.430
Or did I come apart on my own?

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:13.640
If that's the case, maybe
being put together isn't right.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:19.890
No. I'm not supposed to be in pieces.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:32.180
Even though I'm not perfectly together, seems there's no problem as of now...

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:54.640
What's up with this place?

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.140
"I'm in pieces, but they're connected."

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.850
I completely understand the concept now.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:31.510
Still, don't tell me I have to put
all the pieces of this world together.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:44.470
Is it ridiculous to think that I've
been given a role to play in this world?

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.180
Hey!

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:53.220
Excuse me, but where are we?

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:56.180
You up there,

00:04:56.180 --> 00:05:01.550
why is this world chopped into little pieces like this?

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:36.140
In other words, to me, this world isn't right,

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.600
just as it wasn't right for me to be in pieces.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:05.430
Who knows if there's any point to using
the door in a world like this, but here goes.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.890
Kaeru.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:36.720
I don't know this girl, but I do know her name.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.140
It's Kaeru.

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:45.470
And, by remembering her name,
I understand more about myself.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:49.260
My name is... Sakaido.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:54.390
Huh? I can't remember my <i>full </i>name, but it doesn't matter.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.510
What matters is that I'm the brilliant detective.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:07:03.970
And that I must solve the mystery of Kaeru's death.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:21.800
Inspector Momoki, Sakaido has awakened.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:25.470
So he finally survived the fall in the bedroom.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:26.930
How's the id well?

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:28.300
It's stable, sir.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.430
Good. As always, let's be thorough.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:34.760
Togo, take general analysis. Kokufu, assist Togo.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:38.640
Shiratake, ascertain periods and locations.
Habutae, analyze the people.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:41.970
Wakashika, deductions about Kaeru's murder.

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:46.680
The battle lasts until our brilliant detective
solves the mystery of her death.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:50.100
Until then, devote yourselves to
swiftly deciphering information

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:54.890
about our serial killer, the "Perforator,"
from the world of his drive to kill.

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:56.180
Yes, sir!

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:06.970
The door was locked from the inside.
The window was locked, too.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:09.890
No way she gave herself
a single stab to the chest.

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.100
This ain't no period drama.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.890
That makes this a locked-room mystery.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:21.600
Oh, wait. There are no rooms here.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:27.640
Hmm, now what? Puzzles
exist to be solved... supposedly.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:31.600
Even my seemingly dysfunctional elbow must have a purpose...

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:47.430
Sakaido is on the move.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:48.930
Entering a room.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:52.050
Information volume is
about to surge. Stay vigilant.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:06.350
The books are all actual titles.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.470
Any rare volumes?

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:14.010
Several out of print. But nothing
that could identify the Perforator.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:16.010
Habutae, the people in the pictures.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:17.760
Beginning analysis.

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:22.760
The family that lives here?

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:25.180
Pro tennis players and actors.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:27.300
All well known via TV and the internet.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:31.050
Unlikely to be personally connected to the killer.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:37.100
But normally, people in framed
pictures are very close friends or family.

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:38.930
In the real world, yeah.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.850
Id wells are the human unconscious.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:45.140
Anything goes in the mind.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:47.180
This calendar...

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:53.850
The dates and days of the week
align perfectly with March 2019.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.390
A rare occurrence.

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:58.510
Human memory really exhibits variation.

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:00.930
Then did something happen in that month?

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:02.640
Not necessarily.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:08.350
Exactly. When you draw information
from the well, don't rush to conclusions.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:13.220
All information is valuable.
Don't try to assign meaning yourself.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:15.680
Let the meaning rise to the surface.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:25.260
The id well... I can't believe such detailed memories

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:29.220
are hidden in a world formed from the drive to kill.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:31.640
Don't space out, Hondomachi.

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:34.260
Focus on the rhythm of the well-side staff.

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:36.640
Sorry, Mr. Matsuoka.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:44.050
The thing floating in the center there
is what the Mizuhanome is generating--

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:47.220
the world of the Perforator's impulse to kill, right?

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:52.680
Yes. In total, five Perforator
victims have been discovered.

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:56.720
We detected the Perforator's
cognition particles at each crime scene.

00:10:56.720 --> 00:11:01.220
But... he kills by drilling holes in people's heads,

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:05.100
and yet his drive to kill creates a disjointed jigsaw world.

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:10.220
Well, the intent to kill is basically
the impulse portion of things.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:13.010
When they consciously
consider the murder method,

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:15.510
it diverges greatly from the well.

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:20.140
Mr. Matsuoka, have you ever wanted to enter one yourself? A well, I mean.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:24.140
Hell no. Only someone who's killed can enter a well.

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:29.260
What's more, to really perform as the
brilliant detective takes a special aptitude.

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:30.550
Oh?

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:36.600
Just as you said, that world is essentially the serial killer's impulse to kill.

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:41.550
To go above and beyond, the brilliant
detective's got to have a few screws loose.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:45.220
The calendar from earlier
seems to have been a gift.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:49.720
It's faint, but it bears the name
"Fujita's Wares" and an address.

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:50.850
Mr. Matsuoka.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.180
Got the address!

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:56.010
Now it's time for us field
analysts to do our job. Come on.

00:11:57.220 --> 00:12:00.600
Attention: Sakaido is about to encounter people.

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:07.260
I'm coming in.

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:09.970
A visitor.

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:11.300
Hello, sir.

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:13.640
Come in. Welcome to our home.

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:14.890
Welcome.

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:16.930
We never have visitors.

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:20.600
Do all of you live here?

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:21.430
Yes.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.140
We <i>are </i>family.

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:27.300
Obara Kenta, Takada Wataru, Imanishi Eiko,

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:30.180
Fujita Yoshihito, Kitamura Masami...

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:34.140
Of the seven, five are victims of the Perforator.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:40.010
How horrific. He's making his victims live under one roof as a family?!

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:44.430
Don't lose your cool.
Anything can happen in the unconscious.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.640
Still, there's a reason for <i>this</i>.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:51.390
We have hits for the remaining two in
the database of missing persons reports.

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:54.600
Kazuta Haruka and Oonuki Yuji.

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:57.050
In other words, these two are already...

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:58.100
Don't be so sure.

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:02.760
That's right. The report for
Oonuki Yuji was filed yesterday.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:08.600
The Perforator seems to confine his victims
for several days before killing them.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:11.140
They may very well be alive.

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.600
Um.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:18.890
Look here. I hadn't recognized this as
a face, and Sakaido hadn't noticed either.

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:20.970
There's a reflection.

00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:22.800
Sending the image.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:32.850
John Walker.

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:37.140
It can't be... The Perforator had
contact with John Walker, too?

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:47.050
Mr. Matsuoka, we have confirmation.

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:52.300
It seems that fragmented man in the well is definitely Oonuki Yuji after all.

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:57.010
About "Fujita's Wares" from the calendar--
it closed and now the building's vacant.

00:13:57.010 --> 00:14:01.010
But this is only 15 minutes from
the Oonuki residence on foot.

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:04.760
We'll retrace Oonuki Yuji's
steps on the day of his abduction

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:06.930
and look for cognition particles.

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:07.760
Understood.

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:12.800
You'll probably enter the Perforator's
area of operation, so exercise caution.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:17.430
I can drive, you know.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:21.350
I have no desire to be a
passenger with a rookie driver.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:25.180
More importantly, watch the Wakumusubi.

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:29.300
The Wakumusubi... You know, it's funny.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:33.680
To think this machine can
detect people's intent to kill.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:37.390
You know how we write "ido"
in reference to the well?

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:43.550
Is the dad joke on Freud's "id" and the
Japanese word for "well" intentional?

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:45.470
Or is it a coincidence?

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:48.300
It's no dad joke. It's fate.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:49.850
"Fate"?

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:53.390
"Ido" can also be written
with "other" and "earth."

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:55.260
Simply put, an "otherworld."

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:57.010
Oh, you're right.

00:14:57.010 --> 00:15:00.680
With all those meanings, it was meant to be.

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:04.260
Who is this girl?

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:05.930
I've never seen her.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:08.760
She's not a member of our family.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:12.260
She's a visitor who just barged in, like you.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:15.800
Just because our home is
open, it's okay to barge in?

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:17.430
It's not okay.

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:20.970
But there's something wrong about her.

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:23.550
Yeah, there is.

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:27.350
More like there's something wrong about this world.

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:34.720
I guess no one would question the world they live in.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:38.600
But that is precisely
the brilliant detective's job.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:42.010
I have to question the way the world is.

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:47.100
The city.

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:49.390
The puzzle pieces are about to fall into place.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.550
Dammit, Sakaido.

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:15.640
You're the brilliant detective.
Why did you leave the crime scene?

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:20.050
There are countless ways to stab
Kaeru in that wide-open locked room.

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:23.050
We need more material to consider.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:37.100
Kokufu, turn the part he just
completed 90 degrees clockwise!

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:47.220
Now, what did I find?

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:51.010
I have no clue what it means,
but I did learn something.

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:55.180
In this world, there's more meaning
in what's missing than what's not.

00:16:55.180 --> 00:17:01.510
And those meaningful deficiencies
are hidden within the larger picture.

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:05.220
Still, what could "takoya" be?

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:08.050
The logo for Takoyaki House
Pot Octopus matches.

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:11.470
There are four locations
in Chuuou and one in Choufu.

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:14.680
The same neighborhood from the calendar.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:17.050
Mr. Matsuoka is right near there.

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:23.600
An assault team arrives in five minutes.
Stand by until then.

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:28.350
Mr. Matsuoka, these characters are slightly tilted.

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:29.300
Oh?

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:31.350
To see them at this angle...

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:36.680
...you'd have to be...

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:48.010
What was that?

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:00.220
Mr. Matsuoka, the Wakumusubi!

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:05.350
It's Matsuoka. Cognition particles detected.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.220
Pattern matches the Perforator.

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:08.550
Confirmed.

00:18:08.550 --> 00:18:13.010
The link with the Wakumusubi
has already affected the well.

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:20.010
The world is breaking apart again.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:25.050
Or perhaps its natural state is to be in pieces...

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:27.100
Kaeru.

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:38.510
This reading. It indicates a
fresh drive to kill, doesn't it?

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.430
There are two missing persons.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:45.890
He might be pursuing to kill them as we speak!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.220
Mr. Matsuoka!

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:48.930
Stay here. Wait for backup.

00:18:48.930 --> 00:18:52.140
I can't! People just within
reach are about to be killed!

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:53.600
Exactly.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.800
<i>I'm </i>going.

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:59.800
Don't, Matsuoka. Stay on standby.

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:02.010
Resident information located.

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:06.100
The head of household is
Fukuda Tamotsu, 33. No family.

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:07.600
Hey, that's...

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:10.720
Against regulations, yeah.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:13.470
Wait in the car for the assault team.

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:19.510
The world is breaking itself back into pieces.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:23.220
His drive to kill is fragmented,
yet he kills by drilling...

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:25.850
Does that incongruence mean something?

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:34.300
Hey, what are you doing? What do you want?!

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:39.890
Stop! Please stop!

00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:43.140
Don't! Please! Don't!

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:51.550
Aw, shit!

00:19:56.470 --> 00:19:58.050
He's still breathing!

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:00.970
Medical unit, carry the victim out!

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:12.220
This is a fragmented world.

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:15.470
In other words, it's natural to be in pieces.

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:17.390
Even I'm not whole.

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:22.260
But Kaeru has all of her pieces put together.

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:25.260
She ought to have missing parts.

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:28.430
Thus, they must be there.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:30.890
I know you're there.

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:33.390
Leave Kaeru's body!

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:38.350
For real?

00:20:57.470 --> 00:20:58.390
Hmm.

00:20:58.390 --> 00:21:01.680
Sakaido has found Kaeru's killer.

00:21:01.680 --> 00:21:04.220
Now what?

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:06.300
Do I arrest him?

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:12.220
Are there even police and prisons in this fragmented world?

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:15.300
Right. Not much you can do from the well, huh.

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:17.510
Well, it's the same with a mystery.

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:21.100
Arresting the bad guy isn't
the brilliant detective's job.

00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:23.100
He just solves the case.

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:26.890
Inspector Momoki, shall I eject Sakaido?

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:28.390
No, hold off.

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:31.140
Hey! An eighth person showed up!

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:34.720
The incomplete people in the
house. There's a new one!

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:42.140
When the case is finished,
make sure to leave our house, okay?

00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:43.350
Who're you?

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:44.300
It's her!

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:46.260
From the field analyst unit!

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:48.300
How?

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:49.680
Matsuoka, do you copy?

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:51.140
Hondomachi!

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:53.260
Hey!

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:56.010
Respond!

00:21:56.010 --> 00:21:57.970
What's wrong, Hondomachi?
